## TSPEC-Specific Requirements

### Structure Requirements
1. Test Plan Overview
2. Unit Tests (TSPEC.UT.XX)
3. Integration Tests (TSPEC.IT.XX)
4. End-to-End Tests (TSPEC.E2E.XX)
5. Performance Tests (TSPEC.PT.XX)
6. Security Tests (TSPEC.ST.XX)
7. Test Data Requirements

### Test Categories
- **Unit (UT)**: Component isolation tests
- **Integration (IT)**: Module interaction tests
- **End-to-End (E2E)**: Full flow tests
- **Performance (PT)**: Load/stress tests
- **Security (ST)**: Vulnerability tests

### Content Quality
- Clear test objectives
- Preconditions stated
- Test steps detailed
- Expected results defined
- Automation status indicated

### ID Pattern
- Format: `TSPEC.{TYPE}.XX` where TYPE is test category
- Example: `TSPEC.IT.03` (Integration test, third case)

### Test Case Format
```yaml
TSPEC.UT.XX:
  name: [Test Case Name]
  category: unit|integration|e2e|performance|security
  priority: P0|P1|P2
  automation: automated|manual|pending
  description: |
    [Test purpose]
  preconditions:
    - [Precondition 1]
  test_data:
    input: [Test input data]
    expected: [Expected output]
  steps:
    - step: [Action]
      expected: [Result]
  trace:
    upstream: REQ.XX.YY
    spec: SPEC.XX.YY
  tags:
    - smoke
    - regression
```

### Traceability
- @trace: REQ.XX.YY (requirement coverage)
- @trace: SPEC.XX.YY (specification reference)
- @trace: BDD.XX.YY (behavior scenarios)
